|BASE + MOVE(3)
|-
|OP_2SWAP
|BASE + MOVE(4)
|-
|OP_2ROT
|BASE + MOVE(6)
|-
|OP_TOALTSTACK
|BASE + MOVE(1)
|-
|OP_FROMALTSTACK
|BASE + MOVE(1)
|-
|OP_DEPTH
|BASE + WRITE(length(result))
|-
|OP_SIZE
|BASE + WRITE(length(result))
|}

====Rationale====

These operators copy a stack entry and write to another.

OP_ROLL needs to read its operand, then move the selected entry and every entry above it.  It is the only opcode for which the stack manipulation cost is variable (and, regretfully, non-trivial), so we need to limit it.

